<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Guide / Wiki</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="top-bar"><div class="player-info"><strong><%= user.tag %></strong></div></div>
  <div class="game-layout">
    <nav class="sidebar"><a href="/prison-hall">Prison Hall</a><a href="/guide" class="active">Guide / Wiki</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a><a href="/logout">Sign Out</a></nav>
    <main class="main-content">
      <h2 style="color:#ff6b35;">GUIDE / WIKI</h2>
      <p style="color:#a0a0a0;margin-bottom:20px;">Everything the block will not tell you</p>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card"><h3>THE TICK</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Every 5 minutes HP, NRG, NRV and STM regenerate by 20% of maximum (30% for Kingship VIP). The tick stops all ticks. Bank interest lands every 24 hours.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>CRIMES</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Each crime costs Nerve and requires a total Nerve pool. Higher Speed means better odds. Failures land you in Med Bay or The Hole.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>BATTLES</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">7 Energy. Speed decides who strikes first and whether you double-hit. Damage is 90-110% of STR against 85-105% of DEF, adjusted by Stamina, weapon and armor procs.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>MUGGING & RAIDING</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Mugging costs 10 Nerve and only takes hand cash. Cell raids cost 10 Nerve; crack the combo, take the bank and items — get it wrong and it is The Hole.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>THE YARD</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Move with the arrows. Diagonal steps cost 2 STM. Obstacles cost nothing because you cannot enter them. Dig storage earns for cash and items; the Yard Dealer wanders with his cart.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>ECONOMY</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Bank deposits are level-capped (doubled for VIP) and the balance is lost when you transfer prisons. Jobs pay into the bank daily.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>RULES</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">One inmate per person. No spam, cheating, begging or harassment. Duplicate accounts are merged and blocked from trading and combat.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>CLIMBING</h3><p style="font-size:0.9em;">Ironhold → Stonewall → Pinecrest → Dustbowl → Blackridge. Each block raises the level gate, the cell size and the stakes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</body></html>
